;; p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn — initial typed-shim registry (P1b-prep static slice)
;;
;; Fork: jolt gambit-ffi-inv @ a6852ef8. Companion artifacts:
;;   ffi-call-sites.md  (every construction site, file:line)
;;   CONSUMERS.md       (native consumers' binding surfaces, one row per binding)
;;
;; Design ruling implemented (astra §2): "use typed, generated C shims per call
;; shape, shared across symbols with identical ABI shapes. Each accepts the
;; resolved function address. Signature identity includes argument/result types,
;; calling convention, variadic boundary, and relevant ABI layout. ... a finite
;; precompiled registry cannot claim arbitrary runtime-signature support.
;; Unregistered shapes must raise. Generate the initial registry from the native
;; consumer inventory and test fixtures."
;;
;; SHAPE IDENTITY = {:args [jolt-type ...] :ret jolt-type
;;                   :blocking bool :capture-native-error bool
;;                   :variadic nil | {:fixed-count n :tail [jolt-type ...]}
;;                   :kind :procedure | :callable | :pointer-call
;;                   :entry-convention :normal | :collect-safe   (callables)}
;; Two bindings share a shim iff their shape identity is equal.
;;
;; :disposition values
;;   :shim        a generated C shim is owed by the P2/P3 slice; argument is the
;;                resolved function address; errno variants save errno inside the
;;                shim (astra §2 wrapper sequence) before any conversion/cleanup.
;;   :shim+p2     shape belongs to a named native consumer (jolt-crypto /
;;                jolt-file / jolt-parser); required for the P2/P3 gates.
;;   :platform    fork-stdlib shape the Gambit io/socket lanes need (not part of
;;                the P2/P3 consumer triad but produced by real sites in this fork).
;;   :fixture     produced only by test/chez fixtures today; registration keeps
;;                the refusal data honest, the P1b designer decides whether the
;;                shape ships.
;;   :raise       a site produces it but the Gambit path must DELIBERATELY raise
;;                (message-carrying) per astra's P1 boundary: unqualified
;;                blocking/callable modes, dynamic signature compilation.
;;
;; Type vocabulary = jolt.ffi keyword names (stdlib/jolt/ffi.clj docstring,
;; lines 17-20), marshaled per jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme/ffi.clj ffi-types
;; (16-31) and host/chez/java/ffi.ss ffi-type->chez (685-716). :bool is the
;; ONE-BYTE C99 _Bool (unsigned-8 on the wire, converted at the boundary).

